THE CASE FOR FAIL:
The claim restricts custom builds to scenarios requiring 'real-time' active control loops, asserting that standard trackers are merely 'passive recorders.' This creates a false dichotomy by ignoring the prevalence of existing open-source frameworks (e.g., Ray Tune, Optuna integrated with MLflow) that provide robust active learning and Bayesian optimization capabilities without requiring a custom build. The argument fails because it defines the problem space narrowly around 'tight latency constraints' while overlooking that most 'active learning' in research tolerates the seconds-to-minutes latency of existing plugin-based solutions, meaning the condition for 'mandated' custom development is rarely met in practice for small teams.

THE DEFENCE:
